## Findings and actions (7 October 2026)
- SIP disabled; restore using csrutil enable in macOS Recovery, then verify csrutil status. This is a protection weakness, not proof of malware. (7 October 2026)
- Firewall disabled. Enabling failed because administrator authentication is required. It filters inbound traffic and does not stop an infostealer from uploading secrets. (7 October 2026)
- XProtect launch scans disabled; background scans enabled, version 5366 installed 6 October 2026. Cause of disabled launch scans remains unverified. (7 October 2026)
- Software Update reports no new software available. Gatekeeper and FileVault active; authenticated root active. (7 October 2026)
- 58 installed Chrome extension directories. Coupert, VeePN, Get cookies.txt LOCALLY and Tampermonkey have cookies permissions; VPN Japan has proxy and all-site access. This does not establish malicious behavior or that they are currently enabled. Review and remove unneeded extensions after evidence preservation. (7 October 2026)
- CrossOver, Font Book, ClaudeSync and local ZenRay utilities have ad-hoc signatures. DAVE THE DIVER and Disco Elysium app wrappers unsigned. Signatures alone cannot establish infection; locally patched apps must be distinguished from unknown downloads. (7 October 2026)
- System launch binaries show expected vendor signing identities. Shell/Node launchers do not authenticate scripts they execute. No confirmed malicious persistence found in checked locations. (7 October 2026)
- TCC permissions database inaccessible. Full Disk Access and privileged areas not completely inspected. XProtect log keyword search found no confirmed detection; absence of log evidence cannot clear this Mac. (7 October 2026)
- Download official Malwarebytes installer, verify pkg signature, install with administrator authentication, grant required permissions and run scan. Quarantine confirmed findings, retain report and rescan after restart. (7 October 2026)
- From a trusted device secure primary email, revoke sessions and enable MFA; then Claude, password manager, Apple/Google, financial and developer/cloud accounts. Revoke API tokens and assess SSH keys that were locally accessible. Previously stolen cookies survive local cleanup. (7 October 2026)
- If a stealer is confirmed or confidence cannot be restored, preserve documents and forensic findings then erase and reinstall macOS from Recovery; reinstall apps from official sources instead of restoring all apps, launchers and browser profiles. Requires a verified backup and explicit destructive-action approval. (7 October 2026)
- Other devices used for Claude remain outside this Mac audit. (7 October 2026)

