## Detection verification (7 October 2026)
- ClamAV flags Steam Windows cef.win7x64/libcef.dll and cef.win64/libcef.dll as Win.Packed.Mikey-9859574-0. No automatic deletion, whitelist or quarantine applied. (7 October 2026)
- Authenticode verified with osslsigncode 2.14 against /etc/ssl/cert.pem: both files signed by Valve Corp., valid digests, trusted timestamp, certificate chain and CRL checks; return code 0. Detailed logs saved beside this report. (7 October 2026)
- cef.win7x64 SHA256 45927f2baff5479aef1513af2fa7311a84a27d71b4bf72b47556824408385874; size 219859096 bytes; CRC32 3883597792 matches local Steam manifest. (7 October 2026)
- cef.win64 SHA256 c85bf94462b3c79baeac63823db52d15e116eead71ea414e5d3a112c59e434d3; size 219859608 bytes; CRC32 1553093920 matches local Steam manifest. (7 October 2026)
- Inference: strong evidence these detections are false positives on Valve-signed Chromium libraries, not demonstrated session stealers. Same signature reported on upstream Electron 31.0.1: https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/43180 . The upstream report is supporting context, not proof for these exact hashes. (7 October 2026)
- Mac ClamAV target scan: 99 files, zero detections, one access error. Explicit readability check identifies sole inaccessible target as /Library/Logs/com.sidefx.com/sesinetd.log, a license-server log included from launch arguments; it is not an executable. (7 October 2026)
- GitHub claude-sync and Memory repositories verified PRIVATE through gh repo view. No Claude session or API key matching screened patterns found in inspected claude-sync JSONL files below 15 MB. This bounded check does not establish all logs are secret-free. (7 October 2026)

